    "progress": "PR #23 open. Two proven causes fixed: D4's real-wall-clock 800ms budget (3/6 runs failed under 3-way contention; SLOP_TEST_PERF_SCALE added) and Playwright's hardcoded port 4765 (PortInUseError reproduced; free-port at config load). The OOM/fork-storm theory did NOT reproduce even at load 129 with 384 concurrent spawns — honestly reported, no blind fix; maxWorkers noted as the lever if ever seen on smaller hardware. Same-checkout concurrent gates remain unsafe by design (shared dist/slop) — documented."
